Name the shell natively, in quotes, on the ConPTY command line

startProcess() builds the command line by joining the shell path and its
arguments with spaces. Session::run() (0008) resolves a bare program name
with QStandardPaths::findExecutable(), which answers with forward slashes:

    C:/WINDOWS/system32/cmd.exe /d

cmd.exe parses its own command line, reads the "/c" in "/cmd.exe" as its /c
switch and runs "md .exe /d", so a widget configured with "cmd.exe" gets a
shell that exits at once with "The syntax of the command is incorrect".

Put the path first with native separators, and in quotes, the form
CreateProcess documents for a module name inside lpCommandLine. Unquoted, a
path with spaces still starts the right program, but only because
CreateProcess tries each space-separated prefix in turn, and an existing file
at an earlier prefix would run instead. The arguments are joined as before.

Upstream: not submitted; belongs on PR #578, which is not being merged --
         see 0001's header
Applies-to: all environments (the changed code is behind Q_OS_WIN)

--- a/lib/ptyqt/conptyprocess.cpp
+++ b/lib/ptyqt/conptyprocess.cpp
@@ -129,7 +129,10 @@
     LPWSTR envArg = envV.empty() ? nullptr : envV.data();
 
     QStringList exeAndArgs = arguments;
-    exeAndArgs.prepend(m_shellPath);
+    // Native separators, because cmd.exe reads the "/c" in ".../cmd.exe" as its
+    // /c switch; quotes, because the path may contain spaces.
+    exeAndArgs.prepend(QLatin1Char('"') + QDir::toNativeSeparators(m_shellPath) +
+                       QLatin1Char('"'));
     auto cmdArg = exeAndArgs.join(QLatin1String(" ")).toStdWString();
 
     HRESULT hr{E_UNEXPECTED};
